# Custom shell commands
# These are wrapper scripts this repo generates via writeShellScriptBin (not
# upstream packages) -- source file named in parens. See `installed`'s
# "Custom Bash Wrappers" line for the full file list.

File finding & editing
    vs                      Fuzzy-find a file (fd + fsel) and open it in vim
                             (modules/programs/terminal/custom/vs.nix)
    rgf                     Live ripgrep search through fzf with a bat
                             preview pane; Enter opens the match in nvim at
                             that line (modules/programs/terminal/custom/rgf.nix)

File management (impermanence-aware)
    mv                      Wraps coreutils mv: runs it in the background and
                             pops a progress bar (via `progress`) if it's
                             still running after 0.2s -- useful for large or
                             cross-disk moves that would otherwise look hung
                             (modules/programs/terminal/custom/fileManagement.nix)
    mvd                     Move across disks via rsync --remove-source-files
                             instead of mv, for when moving between
                             filesystems (same file as above)
    ex                      Extract any archive: `unar -d "$@"`
                             (modules/programs/terminal/custom/ex.nix)
    lsp [dir]                eza long-listing of dir's mirror under
                             /persistent -- i.e. what IS preserved across a
                             reboot (modules/programs/terminal/custom/ls.nix)
    treep [dir]              Same as lsp, but as a tree view
    lst [dir]                eza long-listing of dir itself, with anything
                             already under /persistent filtered out -- i.e.
                             what is NOT yet persisted and would be lost on
                             reboot
    treet [dir]              Same as lst, but as a tree view

DNS
    dogs                    `doggo --short "$@"` -- terser doggo output
                             (modules/programs/terminal/custom/doggo.nix)
    dogprop <domain>        Propagation check: queries a domain against
                             8.8.8.8, 9.9.9.9, 1.1.1.1, and its own
                             authoritative nameserver, side by side

Git
    lg                      Loads an ssh-agent with the GitHub deploy key,
                             launches gitui, kills the agent on exit
                             (modules/programs/terminal/gitui.nix)

Docs
    tldr                    Wraps tealdeer: refreshes the local cheat-sheet
                             cache first if it's missing or >7 days old, then
                             shows the page (modules/programs/terminal/tealdeer.nix)

Gaming (all run inside the app-games systemd slice for memory containment;
set OBS_CAP=1 to wrap with obs-gamecapture if OBS is running -- see `info`)
    gmgsmh                  gamescope + gamemode + mangohud -- full dedicated-
                             resolution session (modules/programs/workstation/gui/games/games.nix)
    gmmh                    gamemode + mangohud, no gamescope -- windowed/
                             borderless games
    mh                      mangohud only -- lightweight overlay, no
                             gamemode/gamescope wrapping

Display
    gamma-control {temp-up|temp-down|bright-up|bright-down|reset}
                             Manual driver behind the Alt+Arrows brightness/
                             color-temp keybinds (see `keybinds`); tracks
                             state in /tmp/gamma_state so repeated calls step
                             from the last value (modules/programs/workstation/gui/gammastep.nix)
